<title>ITALY: Ifil 1996 cons net profit rises.</title>
<headline>Ifil 1996 cons net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			339    vs    321</p>
<p>    Ord div				130 lire vs 120 lire</p>
<p>    Savings share div		  150 lire vs 140 lire</p>
<p>Note - Agnelli family holding company Ifil Spa said it would propose to shareholders setting aside a total 100 billion lire to buy back up 20 million of its ordinary and/or savings shares at a minimum price of 1,000 and a maximum price of 10,000.  </p>
<p>    Cons net equity		    3,640    vs  3,430</p>
<p>    Cons net financial position	 50    vs    (26)</p>
<p>    Parent net profit		    138    vs    130</p>
<p>    Parent net equity		  3,562    vs  3,430</p>
<p>Note - Ifil said proceeds from its shareholdings showed a rise of around 18 percent on 1995 and represented 75 percent of the group net profit &quot;confirming the importance of the results of those stakes in formation of Ifil's consolidated profit.&quot;</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +39 266129507</p>
</text>
